This module provides the observability layer of the Smart City IDS.
It aggregates data from every subsystem ‚Äî database, LLM providers,
circuit breakers, deduplication cache, rate limiters, request queue,
and governance engine ‚Äî and exposes it through REST and Prometheus
endpoints.

Endpoint overview:
    GET  /health                   ‚Äì deep component health check
    GET  /api/safety               ‚Äì automation-mode, thresholds, cache
    GET  /api/production-status    ‚Äì rate-limiter/cb/queue health booleans
    GET  /api/pipeline-overview    ‚Äì 5-stage pipeline strip for dashboard
    GET  /api/metrics              ‚Äì aggregate JSON metrics blob
    GET  /api/db/stats             ‚Äì database storage statistics
    GET  /api/deduplicator-stats   ‚Äì dedup cache hit-rate and cost savings
    POST /api/deduplicator/clear   ‚Äì flush dedup cache (auth required)
    GET  /metrics                  ‚Äì Prometheus text exposition format

Design notes:
    * ``_deps()`` lazily imports all shared-state objects and returns them
      in a dict to avoid circular imports at module load time.
    * ``/health`` reuses ``_build_llm_diagnostics()`` from ``api.llm``
      to give a single-call view of the entire system.
    * ``/api/pipeline-overview`` computes per-stage throughput in
      alerts/minute ‚Äî intended for the React dashboard's horizontal
      pipeline strip.
