# ‚îÄ‚îÄ Lazy dependency helpers ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ‚îÄ

def _gov():
    """Lazy-import governance helpers from the ``governance`` module.

    Returns a dict of callables so callers can use ``g["get_mode"]()`` etc.
    Lazy importing avoids circular dependencies at module load time.
    """
    from governance import (
        governance,               # GovernanceEngine singleton
        get_automation_mode,      # ‚Üí str: "autopilot" | "assisted" | "manual"
        set_automation_mode,      # (mode) ‚Üí dict with status
        get_pending_actions,      # ‚Üí list of PendingAction objects
        get_governance_status,    # ‚Üí dict with full dashboard data
        approve_pending_action,   # (id, operator, execute_fn, ‚Ä¶) ‚Üí dict
        reject_pending_action,    # (id, operator, reason) ‚Üí dict
    )
    return {
        "governance": governance,
        "get_mode": get_automation_mode,
        "set_mode": set_automation_mode,
        "pending": get_pending_actions,
        "status": get_governance_status,
        "approve": approve_pending_action,
        "reject": reject_pending_action,
    }


def _deps():
    """Retrieve K8s automation client and database handle from shared state."""
    from api._state import k8s_automation, db
    return k8s_automation, db


