"""LLM diagnostics, circuit-breaker management, and stats export API router.

This module provides deep observability into the multi-provider LLM subsystem.
The Smart City IDS supports up to six LLM providers simultaneously
(xAI Grok, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, Kimi, and a local rule-based
engine).  Each provider can be in one of several states:

    operational     ‚Äì healthy, accepting requests
    not_configured  ‚Äì no API key set for this provider
    cooldown        ‚Äì temporarily paused after an error (auto-recovers)
    error           ‚Äì last call failed (check diagnostics for cause)
    circuit_open    ‚Äì circuit breaker tripped after repeated failures
    recovering      ‚Äì circuit breaker half-open, testing with probe requests

The circuit-breaker pattern prevents cascade failures: when a provider fails
``failure_threshold`` times consecutively, the breaker opens and no further
requests are sent until ``recovery_timeout`` seconds elapse, at which point
a few probe requests test recovery (half-open state).

Endpoints:
    GET  /api/llm/diagnostics       ‚Äì verbose per-provider health (no auth)
    GET  /api/llm/status            ‚Äì compact provider list (auth required)
    POST /api/circuit-breaker/reset ‚Äì manually reset breakers
    GET  /api/circuit-breaker/status ‚Äì breaker state summary
    GET  /api/rate-limiter/status   ‚Äì alert-level rate limiter stats
    POST /api/rate-limiter/reset    ‚Äì reset rate limiter counters
    GET  /api/llm-stats/export      ‚Äì per-engine latency, cost, token stats
"""

