engine).  Each provider can be in one of several states:

    operational     ‚Äì healthy, accepting requests
    not_configured  ‚Äì no API key set for this provider
    cooldown        ‚Äì temporarily paused after an error (auto-recovers)
    error           ‚Äì last call failed (check diagnostics for cause)
    circuit_open    ‚Äì circuit breaker tripped after repeated failures
    recovering      ‚Äì circuit breaker half-open, testing with probe requests

The circuit-breaker pattern prevents cascade failures: when a provider fails
``failure_threshold`` times consecutively, the breaker opens and no further
requests are sent until ``recovery_timeout`` seconds elapse, at which point
a few probe requests test recovery (half-open state).

